## How to answer
First, in `summary`, write one line for every judged invariant and every neighbour, keyed by
its path: what it requires of the fields it shares with the others. Then compare, field by
field, each judged invariant against every other invariant shown, and give in `members` one
entry per judged invariant with every finding it is a side of (an empty list when none). Name
the other side by its path in `with`, give the concrete input, and a one-line fix.
